      "_agent_risk": "Error: Reached max turns (4)",
      "_agent_requirements": "Error: Reached max turns (4)",
      "_agent_explorer": "Now I have a comprehensive understanding. Here is my analysis:\n\n---\n\n## AUT-8425: Reusable Code & Root Cause Analysis\n\n### Root Cause: Continuous Polling with No Termination Condition\n\nThe defect is caused by **unbounded polling loops** — the frontend keeps calling APIs every 5 seconds indefinitely when a job's status never reaches a terminal state (`completed`, `failed`, `error`). There are **two distinct polling mechanisms** in the filing flow, both lacking max-retry limits.\n\n---\n\n### Bug Location #1: `usePolling` hook — no max retry\n\n**File:** `libs/helpers/src/hooks/usePolling.tsx`\n\n```\nusePolling({ callback, delay = 5000 })\n```\n\n- Schedules a `setTimeout` to call the callback after `delay` ms.\n- **No `maxRetries` or `maxDuration` parameter** — if consumers keep calling `startPolling()`, it continues forever.\n- Used in 3 places, all with the same bug pattern: `startPolling()` called **in the render body** (not in `useEffect`), creating an infinite chain: render → startPolling → 5s → reCallAPI → re-render → startPolling → ...\n\n**Consumers with identical bug pattern (polling called in render body):**\n\n| File | Line |\n|------|------|\n| `libs/entp/src/lib/reports/GstReport/DownloadView/index.tsx` | 94–105 |\n| `libs/entp/src/lib/reconcile/RecoDownloadReports/index.tsx` | 101–112 |\n| `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/ImportData/DownloadData/index.tsx` | 46–57 |\n\nAll three check `isIncomplete` (any item status not in `completed`/`failed`/`error`), then call `startPolling()` unconditionally during render.\n\n---\n\n### Bug Location #2: `UploadGSTR1Data` — `setInterval` with faulty cleanup\n\n**File:** `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Gstr1/UploadData/index.tsx:141-155`\n\n```typescript\nlet timer: NodeJS.Timer;  // Module-level (shared across instances!)\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (uploadId) {\n    getUploadStatus(uploadId);\n    timer = setInterval(() => {\n      getUploadStatus(uploadId);\n    }, 1000 * 5);\n  } else {\n    if (timer) clearInterval(timer as unknown as number);\n  }\n  return () => {\n    if (timer && !uploadId) clearInterval(timer as unknown as number);\n    //           ^^^^^^^^^^  BUG: only clears if uploadId is null\n  };\n}, [uploadId, getUploadStatus]);\n```\n\n**Issues:**\n1. Cleanup function only clears interval when `!uploadId` — if component unmounts while `uploadId` is set, interval keeps running.\n2. `timer` is module-level, not component-scoped — shared across instances.\n3. No max retry count — polls forever if status never becomes `done`.\n\n---\n\n### Bug Location #3: `FileReturnGSTR1` — no progress feedback\n\n**File:** `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Gstr1/FileReturnGSTR1/index.tsx:109-141`\n\nThe `onSubmitFIle` function calls `postDataApi('gst-returns/gstr/proceed-file/', ...)` as a single POST. If the backend creates a job (referenced by the \"Main job id\" in the ticket), the frontend has **no polling mechanism** to track job completion, so it appears stuck.\n\n---\n\n### Reusable Code for the Fix\n\n#### 1. `usePolling` hook (to be enhanced)\n- **Path:** `libs/helpers/src/hooks/usePolling.tsx`\n- **What to reuse:** The existing hook structure — add `maxRetries` and/or `maxDuration` params.\n- **How:** Add a retry counter ref and stop polling after N attempts or T seconds.\n\n#### 2. `useGetDataApi` hook\n- **Path:** `libs/helpers/src/hooks/APIHooks.tsx`\n- **What to reuse:** The `reCallAPI` method for re-fetching data.\n- **How:** All 3 `usePolling` consumers use `reCallAPI` as the callback — this stays the same.\n\n#### 3. Status check pattern (reuse across all consumers)\n- **Pattern:**\n  ```typescript\n  const isIncomplete = apiData?.data?.some((item) => {\n    const normalizedStatus = item.status.toLowerCase();\n    return (\n      normalizedStatus !== 'completed' &&\n      normalizedStatus !== 'failed' &&\n      normalizedStatus !== 'error'\n    );\n  });\n  ```\n- **Used in:** `GstDownloadView`, `RecoDownloadReports`, `DownloadReports`\n- **How:** Keep the pattern but move `startPolling()` call into a `useEffect` instead of the render body.\n\n#### 4. `infoViewContext` (error/success notification)\n- **Path:** `libs/helpers/src/context/AppInfoViewContext/`\n- **What to reuse:** `useInfoViewActionsContext()` → `fetchError()` / `showMessage()`\n- **How:** Show a user-facing message when polling reaches max retries (\"Job is taking longer than expected, please refresh manually\").\n\n#### 5. `AppRefreshIcon` + manual refresh button pattern\n- **Path:** `libs/icons` (`AppRefreshIcon`)\n- **What to reuse:** All 3 polling components already have a manual \"Refresh\" button. If polling stops after max retries, the user can still manually refresh.\n\n#### 6. `getUploadStatus` pattern (UploadData)\n- **Path:** `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Gstr1/UploadData/index.tsx:53-90`\n- **What to reuse:** The `getDataApi('gst-returns/gstr1/upload-status/', ...)` call pattern.\n- **How:** Fix the `useEffect` cleanup to always clear the interval, and add a max retry counter.\n\n#### 7. `FileReturnGSTR1` / `CommonModules/FileReturns` — proceed-file flow\n- **Paths:**\n  - `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Gstr1/FileReturnGSTR1/index.tsx` (GSTR1-specific)\n  - `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/CommonModules/FileReturns/index.tsx` (generic, config-driven)\n  - `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Gstr6/FileReturnGSTR6/index.tsx`\n  - `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Gstr9/FileReturnGSTR9/index.tsx`\n  - `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Itc04/FileReturnITC04/index.tsx`\n  - `libs/smb/src/lib/tds/forms/forms/FileForm/index.tsx`\n- **What to reuse:** The `onSubmitFile`/`onSubmitFIle` function that calls `gst-returns/gstr/proceed-file/`.\n- **How:** If the backend returns a `job_id`, add polling to track job completion.\n\n#### 8. `useExpireTime` hook (countdown timer pattern)\n- **Path:** `libs/helpers/src/hooks/useExpireTime.tsx`\n- **What to reuse:** As a reference for implementing a max-duration timeout for polling.\n\n#### 9. `Gstr1/index.tsx` — the orchestrating page\n- **Path:** `apps/enterprise/src/app/GSTReturn/Gstr1/index.tsx`\n- **What to reuse:** Shows how `FileReturnGSTR1` and `UploadGSTR1Data` are rendered in tabs.\n- **How:** The tab-based rendering means both upload polling AND file-return polling can be active simultaneously.\n\n#### 10. Return configuration\n- **Path:** `apps/enterprise/src/app/GSTReturn/config/returnConfig.ts`\n- **What to reuse:** The `returnConfigs` array defines all return types and their steps. The filing step (`File Return`) is the last step for each return type.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Recommended Fixes\n\n1. **Enhance `usePolling` hook** with `maxRetries` (default ~60 = 5 min at 5s intervals) and a `stopPolling` return function.\n2. **Move `startPolling()` calls into `useEffect`** in all 3 consumer components instead of calling in render body.\n3. **Fix `UploadGSTR1Data` cleanup** — always clear interval on unmount regardless of `uploadId`; move `timer` to a `useRef`.\n4. **Add timeout feedback** — show message to user when polling stops after max retries.",
      "_agent_analysis": "Error: Reached max turns (4)\n\nNow I have a comprehensive understanding. Here is my analysis:\n\n---\n\n## AUT-8425: Reusable Code & Root Cause Analysis\n\n### Root Cause: Continuous Polling with No Termination Condition\n\nThe defect is caused by **unbounded polling loops** — the frontend keeps calling APIs every 5 seconds indefinitely when a job's status never reaches a terminal state (`completed`, `failed`, `error`). There are **two distinct polling mechanisms** in the filing flow, both lacking max-retry limits.\n\n---\n\n### Bug Location #1: `usePolling` hook — no max retry\n\n**File:** `libs/helpers/src/hooks/usePolling.tsx`\n\n```\nusePolling({ callback, delay = 5000 })\n```\n\n- Schedules a `setTimeout` to call the callback after `delay` ms.\n- **No `maxRetries` or `maxDuration` parameter** — if consumers keep calling `startPolling()`, it continues forever.\n- Used in 3 places, all with the same bug pattern: `startPolling()` called **in the render body** (not in `useEffect`), creating an infinite chain: render → startPolling → 5s → reCallAPI → re-render → startPolling → ...\n\n**Consumers with identical bug pattern (polling called in render body):**\n\n| File | Line |\n|------|------|\n| `libs/entp/src/lib/reports/GstReport/DownloadView/index.tsx` | 94–105 |\n| `libs/entp/src/lib/reconcile/RecoDownloadReports/index.tsx` | 101–112 |\n| `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/ImportData/DownloadData/index.tsx` | 46–57 |\n\nAll three check `isIncomplete` (any item status not in `completed`/`failed`/`error`), then call `startPolling()` unconditionally during render.\n\n---\n\n### Bug Location #2: `UploadGSTR1Data` — `setInterval` with faulty cleanup\n\n**File:** `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Gstr1/UploadData/index.tsx:141-155`\n\n```typescript\nlet timer: NodeJS.Timer;  // Module-level (shared across instances!)\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (uploadId) {\n    getUploadStatus(uploadId);\n    timer = setInterval(() => {\n      getUploadStatus(uploadId);\n    }, 1000 * 5);\n  } else {\n    if (timer) clearInterval(timer as unknown as number);\n  }\n  return () => {\n    if (timer && !uploadId) clearInterval(timer as unknown as number);\n    //           ^^^^^^^^^^  BUG: only clears if uploadId is null\n  };\n}, [uploadId, getUploadStatus]);\n```\n\n**Issues:**\n1. Cleanup function only clears interval when `!uploadId` — if component unmounts while `uploadId` is set, interval keeps running.\n2. `timer` is module-level, not component-scoped — shared across instances.\n3. No max retry count — polls forever if status never becomes `done`.\n\n---\n\n### Bug Location #3: `FileReturnGSTR1` — no progress feedback\n\n**File:** `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Gstr1/FileReturnGSTR1/index.tsx:109-141`\n\nThe `onSubmitFIle` function calls `postDataApi('gst-returns/gstr/proceed-file/', ...)` as a single POST. If the backend creates a job (referenced by the \"Main job id\" in the ticket), the frontend has **no polling mechanism** to track job completion, so it appears stuck.\n\n---\n\n### Reusable Code for the Fix\n\n#### 1. `usePolling` hook (to be enhanced)\n- **Path:** `libs/helpers/src/hooks/usePolling.tsx`\n- **What to reuse:** The existing hook structure — add `maxRetries` and/or `maxDuration` params.\n- **How:** Add a retry counter ref and stop polling after N attempts or T seconds.\n\n#### 2. `useGetDataApi` hook\n- **Path:** `libs/helpers/src/hooks/APIHooks.tsx`\n- **What to reuse:** The `reCallAPI` method for re-fetching data.\n- **How:** All 3 `usePolling` consumers use `reCallAPI` as the callback — this stays the same.\n\n#### 3. Status check pattern (reuse across all consumers)\n- **Pattern:**\n  ```typescript\n  const isIncomplete = apiData?.data?.some((item) => {\n    const normalizedStatus = item.status.toLowerCase();\n    return (\n      normalizedStatus !== 'completed' &&\n      normalizedStatus !== 'failed' &&\n      normalizedStatus !== 'error'\n    );\n  });\n  ```\n- **Used in:** `GstDownloadView`, `RecoDownloadReports`, `DownloadReports`\n- **How:** Keep the pattern but move `startPolling()` call into a `useEffect` instead of the render body.\n\n#### 4. `infoViewContext` (error/success notification)\n- **Path:** `libs/helpers/src/context/AppInfoViewContext/`\n- **What to reuse:** `useInfoViewActionsContext()` → `fetchError()` / `showMessage()`\n- **How:** Show a user-facing message when polling reaches max retries (\"Job is taking longer than expected, please refresh manually\").\n\n#### 5. `AppRefreshIcon` + manual refresh button pattern\n- **Path:** `libs/icons` (`AppRefreshIcon`)\n- **What to reuse:** All 3 polling components already have a manual \"Refresh\" button. If polling stops after max retries, the user can still manually refresh.\n\n#### 6. `getUploadStatus` pattern (UploadData)\n- **Path:** `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Gstr1/UploadData/index.tsx:53-90`\n- **What to reuse:** The `getDataApi('gst-returns/gstr1/upload-status/', ...)` call pattern.\n- **How:** Fix the `useEffect` cleanup to always clear the interval, and add a max retry counter.\n\n#### 7. `FileReturnGSTR1` / `CommonModules/FileReturns` — proceed-file flow\n- **Paths:**\n  - `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Gstr1/FileReturnGSTR1/index.tsx` (GSTR1-specific)\n  - `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/CommonModules/FileReturns/index.tsx` (generic, config-driven)\n  - `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Gstr6/FileReturnGSTR6/index.tsx`\n  - `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Gstr9/FileReturnGSTR9/index.tsx`\n  - `libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Itc04/FileReturnITC04/index.tsx`\n  - `libs/smb/src/lib/tds/forms/forms/FileForm/index.tsx`\n- **What to reuse:** The `onSubmitFile`/`onSubmitFIle` function that calls `gst-returns/gstr/proceed-file/`.\n- **How:** If the backend returns a `job_id`, add polling to track job completion.\n\n#### 8. `useExpireTime` hook (countdown timer pattern)\n- **Path:** `libs/helpers/src/hooks/useExpireTime.tsx`\n- **What to reuse:** As a reference for implementing a max-duration timeout for polling.\n\n#### 9. `Gstr1/index.tsx` — the orchestrating page\n- **Path:** `apps/enterprise/src/app/GSTReturn/Gstr1/index.tsx`\n- **What to reuse:** Shows how `FileReturnGSTR1` and `UploadGSTR1Data` are rendered in tabs.\n- **How:** The tab-based rendering means both upload polling AND file-return polling can be active simultaneously.\n\n#### 10. Return configuration\n- **Path:** `apps/enterprise/src/app/GSTReturn/config/returnConfig.ts`\n- **What to reuse:** The `returnConfigs` array defines all return types and their steps. The filing step (`File Return`) is the last step for each return type.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Recommended Fixes\n\n1. **Enhance `usePolling` hook** with `maxRetries` (default ~60 = 5 min at 5s intervals) and a `stopPolling` return function.\n2. **Move `startPolling()` calls into `useEffect`** in all 3 consumer components instead of calling in render body.\n3. **Fix `UploadGSTR1Data` cleanup** — always clear interval on unmount regardless of `uploadId`; move `timer` to a `useRef`.\n4. **Add timeout feedback** — show message to user when polling stops after max retries.\n\nError: Reached max turns (4)",
