      "_security_result": "## Security Audit — AUT-8425\n\n### Changes Summary\n\nAll three files (Gstr1, Gstr6, Gstr7 UploadData) apply the same fix:\n1. Replace module-level `let timer: NodeJS.Timer` with component-scoped `useRef`\n2. Add `MAX_POLL_COUNT = 120` to cap polling at 120 iterations (10 min at 5s intervals)\n3. Stop polling on `'failed'` and `'error'` statuses (previously only stopped on `'done'`)\n4. Proper interval cleanup in the `useEffect` return\n\n### Security Checklist\n\n| # | Check | Result | Notes |\n|---|-------|--------|-------|\n| 1 | **XSS** | OK | Alert messages rendered via JSX `{alertMessage}` — React auto-escapes. No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. |\n| 2 | **Injection** | OK | `id` passed as query param object `{ id }` to `getDataApi`, not string-concatenated into URLs. Axios handles encoding. |\n| 3 | **Auth/Permissions** | OK | No auth changes. Permission checks (`isPermissionAllowed`) remain. API calls use standard `getDataApi` with auth interceptors. |\n| 4 | **Exposed secrets** | OK | No hardcoded keys, tokens, or passwords. |\n| 5 | **Input validation** | OK | `upload_id` from `sessionStorage` (same-origin, app-controlled). Server-side should validate the ID. No new user-input surfaces. |\n| 6 | **Data Isolation** | OK | No cross-tenant concerns. Standard API hooks with business context. |\n| 7 | **PII Handling** | OK | No PII logged or exposed. Error messages from API displayed in UI only. |\n| 8 | **Product Scope** | OK | No cross-product data leakage. Each component uses its own API endpoint (`gstr1/`, `gstr6/`, `gstr7/`). |\n\n### Security Improvements in This Change\n\n- **Client-side DoS fix**: The old code polled indefinitely if the server never returned `'done'` — infinite API calls with no termination. The new `MAX_POLL_COUNT = 120` properly bounds this.\n- **Shared-state race condition fix**: The old module-level `let timer` was shared across all component instances, causing potential timer interference. The new `useRef` properly scopes to each instance.\n- **Terminal state handling**: Now stops polling on `'failed'`/`'error'` in addition to `'done'`, preventing unnecessary API calls when the server has already reported failure.\n\n### No Issues Found\n\nThe changes are purely a stability and resource-management improvement. No new security vulnerabilities are introduced.\n\nVERDICT: PASS",
      "_reviewer_result": "## Code Review: AUT-8425 — Upload polling fix\n\n### Changes Summary\nAll 4 files apply the same fix to the upload status polling mechanism:\n\n1. **Replace module-level `let timer` with instance-scoped `useRef`** — Fixes a bug where a module-scoped timer variable was shared across component instances\n2. **Add `MAX_POLL_COUNT = 120` cap** — Stops polling after 120 iterations (10 minutes), directly addressing the \"continuous API calls and no completion\" issue\n3. **Handle `'failed'` and `'error'` statuses** — Previously only `'done'` stopped polling; now `'failed'`/`'error'` also terminate it\n4. **Fix cleanup logic** — Old cleanup was buggy (conditional `clearInterval` with `!uploadId` check); new cleanup properly clears on every unmount/re-run\n\n### Issues Found\n\n**1. Unplanned file modified (LOW)**\n`libs/smb/src/lib/gst/CommonModules/UploadData/index.tsx` is modified (staged) but not listed in the approved plan's \"Changed files\" section. The change is the same fix applied consistently, so this is reasonable — but it's a plan deviation.\n\n**2. Pre-existing: commented-out code in Gstr6 (INFO)**\nLines 186-189 and 203 in Gstr6 have commented-out code (`// selectedIds`, `// refreshData`, `// tabBarExtraContent`). These are pre-existing, not introduced by this PR — noting for future cleanup.\n\n**3. Pre-existing: unused imports in Gstr1 (INFO)**\n`useCurrentBusiness`, `useUserPermission` are imported but appear unused. Pre-existing issue.\n\n**4. Pre-existing: empty `useCallback` dependency arrays (INFO)**\n`getUploadStatus` in all files uses `useCallback((id) => { ... }, [])` with an empty dependency array despite capturing `infoViewContext` and other values from closure. Pre-existing, not introduced by this change.\n\n### Correctness Verification\n\n- **Timer race condition**: When `MAX_POLL_COUNT` is reached, `setUploadId(null)` triggers a re-render and the effect cleanup fires `clearInterval`. Between state update and cleanup, any interval callback will hit the same `>= MAX_POLL_COUNT` guard and `return` early — no extra API calls. Correct.\n- **Gstr7 consistency**: Gstr7 doesn't call `setReloadPendingUpload(true)` on timeout because it doesn't have that state variable at all — consistent with its own pattern.\n- **All 4 files use identical polling pattern** — `MAX_POLL_COUNT = 120`, `5-second interval`, `useRef` for timer and count. Consistent.\n\n### No Issues Found For\n- Reuse violations — no new components/utils/hooks created\n- Generic VITE_PRODUCT_ID checks — none present\n- Missing imports or broken references — all clean\n- Unnecessary new files — no new files\n- Security concerns — none\n\nVERDICT: PASS",
