      "_ac_agent_result": "Here is my AC verification:\n\n---\n\n## AC Verification Results\n\n**AC: \"Proceed to file sometimes taking too long and no processing/completing. API being called continuously.\"**\n\nThis is a single bug report with two symptoms: (1) upload processing never completes, and (2) the upload-status polling API is called indefinitely.\n\n### Root Causes Identified & Fixed\n\n**1. Missing terminal status handling** → **PASS**\nPreviously, only `status === 'done'` stopped polling. If the backend returned `'failed'` or `'error'`, polling continued forever. All 4 files now check for `done || failed || error` to stop the interval.\n\n**2. No maximum poll limit** → **PASS**\nA `MAX_POLL_COUNT = 120` constant was added (120 polls × 5s interval = 10 min max). After 120 polls, the interval is cleared, `uploadId` is nulled, and `sessionStorage` is cleaned up. This guarantees polling eventually stops even if the backend never returns a terminal status.\n\n**3. Module-level timer variable (memory leak / stale reference)** → **PASS**\nThe old code used `let timer: NodeJS.Timer` at module scope, which is shared across component instances and re-renders — a common source of interval leaks. Replaced with `useRef<ReturnType<typeof setInterval>>` scoped to the component instance.\n\n**4. Buggy cleanup logic** → **PASS**\nOld cleanup: `if (timer && !uploadId) clearInterval(timer)` — the `!uploadId` condition prevented cleanup when the effect re-ran with a new uploadId (old interval leaked). New cleanup unconditionally clears the interval ref in the useEffect return.\n\n### Files Changed\n\n| File | Fix Applied |\n|---|---|\n| `Gstr1/UploadData/index.tsx` | All 4 fixes |\n| `Gstr6/UploadData/index.tsx` | All 4 fixes |\n| `Gstr7/UploadData/index.tsx` | All 4 fixes |\n| `CommonModules/UploadData/index.tsx` | All 4 fixes |\n\n### Unrelated Changes\n- `package.json`: Added `@playwright/test`, `jest-canvas-mock`, `jest-environment-jsdom` — dev dependency additions, not related to the AC.\n- `eslint.config.cjs`: New file — not related to the AC.\n\n### Concerns\n- No unit tests were added or modified to validate the polling-limit behavior.\n- The `MAX_POLL_COUNT` when exceeded silently stops polling without user notification — the user may not know why the upload \"stopped.\" A timeout message/notification would improve UX, but this is an enhancement, not a blocker.\n\n---\n\n**AC: Proceed to file sometimes taking too long / API called continuously → PASS**: The continuous polling is fixed via max poll count (120), handling of `failed`/`error` terminal statuses, proper `useRef`-based interval management, and correct cleanup.\n\n**OVERALL: PASS**",
      "_ac_verification": "Here is my AC verification:\n\n---\n\n## AC Verification Results\n\n**AC: \"Proceed to file sometimes taking too long and no processing/completing. API being called continuously.\"**\n\nThis is a single bug report with two symptoms: (1) upload processing never completes, and (2) the upload-status polling API is called indefinitely.\n\n### Root Causes Identified & Fixed\n\n**1. Missing terminal status handling** → **PASS**\nPreviously, only `status === 'done'` stopped polling. If the backend returned `'failed'` or `'error'`, polling continued forever. All 4 files now check for `done || failed || error` to stop the interval.\n\n**2. No maximum poll limit** → **PASS**\nA `MAX_POLL_COUNT = 120` constant was added (120 polls × 5s interval = 10 min max). After 120 polls, the interval is cleared, `uploadId` is nulled, and `sessionStorage` is cleaned up. This guarantees polling eventually stops even if the backend never returns a terminal status.\n\n**3. Module-level timer variable (memory leak / stale reference)** → **PASS**\nThe old code used `let timer: NodeJS.Timer` at module scope, which is shared across component instances and re-renders — a common source of interval leaks. Replaced with `useRef<ReturnType<typeof setInterval>>` scoped to the component instance.\n\n**4. Buggy cleanup logic** → **PASS**\nOld cleanup: `if (timer && !uploadId) clearInterval(timer)` — the `!uploadId` condition prevented cleanup when the effect re-ran with a new uploadId (old interval leaked). New cleanup unconditionally clears the interval ref in the useEffect return.\n\n### Files Changed\n\n| File | Fix Applied |\n|---|---|\n| `Gstr1/UploadData/index.tsx` | All 4 fixes |\n| `Gstr6/UploadData/index.tsx` | All 4 fixes |\n| `Gstr7/UploadData/index.tsx` | All 4 fixes |\n| `CommonModules/UploadData/index.tsx` | All 4 fixes |\n\n### Unrelated Changes\n- `package.json`: Added `@playwright/test`, `jest-canvas-mock`, `jest-environment-jsdom` — dev dependency additions, not related to the AC.\n- `eslint.config.cjs`: New file — not related to the AC.\n\n### Concerns\n- No unit tests were added or modified to validate the polling-limit behavior.\n- The `MAX_POLL_COUNT` when exceeded silently stops polling without user notification — the user may not know why the upload \"stopped.\" A timeout message/notification would improve UX, but this is an enhancement, not a blocker.\n\n---\n\n**AC: Proceed to file sometimes taking too long / API called continuously → PASS**: The continuous polling is fixed via max poll count (120), handling of `failed`/`error` terminal statuses, proper `useRef`-based interval management, and correct cleanup.\n\n**OVERALL: PASS**",
      "_ac_retry_count": 0,
      "_ac_verified": true,
      "_test_phase_complete": true,
      "original_files": {
        "libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Gstr1/UploadData/index.tsx": "import { useInfoViewActionsContext } from '@mi/context/AppInfoViewContextProvider';\nimport { useCurrentBusiness, useUserPermission } from '@mi/hooks/AuthHooks';\nimport { Form, notification } from 'antd';\nimport { Key, useCallback, useEffect, useMemo, useState } from 'react';\nimport { Beforeunload } from 'react-beforeunload';\nimport TabBadge from '../../components/TabBadge';\nimport CompareData from './CompareData';\nimport {\n  UploadDataContainer,\n  UploadDataNotificationContainer,\n} from './index.styled';\nimport PendingUpload from './PendingUpload';\nimport UploadHistory from './UploadHistory';\n\nimport AppTabs from '@mi/components/AppTabs';\nimport AppViewWrapper from '@mi/components/AppViewWrapper';\nimport { APPModules } from '@mi/constants/AppEnums';\nimport { getDataApi } from '@mi/hooks/APIHooks';\nimport useManagePermission from '@mi/hooks/useManagePermission';\nimport { UploadStatusProps } from '@mi/models/GstReturns/Gstr1/Prepare';\nimport { GSTR1Access } from '@mi/permissions/returns/GSTR1';\nimport { useUploadDataContext } from './Context/UploadDataContext';\n\nlet timer: NodeJS.Timer;\n\nexport type FilterProps = {\n  search: string;\n  invoice_type: string | null;\n};\n\ntype Props = {\n  isGstr1A?: boolean;\n  isButtonDisabled?: boolean;\n};\nexport const UploadGSTR1Data = ({\n  isGstr1A = false,\n  isButtonDisabled,\n}: Props) => {\n  const infoViewContext = useInfoViewActionsContext();\n  const [selectedIds, setSelectedIds] = useState<Key[]>([]);\n  const [activeTab, setActiveTab] = useState('pending_upload');\n  const [tabCount, setTabsCount] = useState<number | null>(null);\n  const [invoiceType, setInvoiceType] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  const [viewType, setViewType] = useState('invoice');\n  const [uploadId, setUploadId] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  const [filterData, setFilterData] = useState<FilterProps | null>(null);\n  const [reloadPendingUpload, setReloadPendingUpload] = useState(false);\n  const [successAlerts, setSuccessAlerts] = useState<string[]>([]);\n  const [errorAlerts, setErrorAlerts] = useState<string[]>([]);\n  const [api, contextHolder] = notification.useNotification();\n  const [form] = Form.useForm();\n  const { isPermissionAllowed } = useManagePermission();\n  const getUploadStatus = useCallback((id: string) => {\n    getDataApi<UploadStatusProps>(\n      'gst-returns/gstr1/upload-status/',\n      infoViewContext,\n      { id, data_type: isGstr1A ? 'GSTR1A' : null },\n      true,\n    )\n      .then((response) => {\n        if (response.data.status === 'done') {\n          setUploadId(null);\n          setReloadPendingUpload(true);\n          sessionStorage.removeItem('upload_id');\n          const success: string[] = [];\n          const errors: string[] = [];\n\n          response.data?.alerts?.forEach((alert) => {\n            if (alert?.status) {\n              success.push(\n                `${alert?.invoice_type?.toUpperCase()}: ${alert?.message}`,\n              );\n            } else {\n              errors.push(\n                `${alert?.invoice_type?.toUpperCase()}: ${alert?.message}`,\n              );\n            }\n          });\n\n          setSuccessAlerts(success);\n          setErrorAlerts(errors);\n        }\n      })\n      .catch((error) => {\n        infoViewContext.fetchError(error.message);\n        setUploadId(null);\n        setReloadPendingUpload(true);\n        sessionStorage.removeItem('upload_id');\n      });\n  }, []);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const upload_id = sessionStorage.getItem('upload_id');\n    if (upload_id) setUploadId(upload_id);\n  }, []);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (reloadPendingUpload) {\n      setTimeout(() => {\n        setReloadPendingUpload(false);\n      }, 1000);\n    }\n  }, [reloadPendingUpload]);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (successAlerts.length > 0)\n      api.success({\n        message: 'Success',\n        description: (\n          <UploadDataNotificationContainer>\n            {successAlerts.map((alertMessage, index) => (\n              <p key={index}>{alertMessage}</p>\n            ))}\n          </UploadDataNotificationContainer>\n        ),\n        duration: 0,\n        onClose: () => setSuccessAlerts([]),\n      });\n  }, [successAlerts]);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (errorAlerts.length > 0)\n      api.error({\n        message: 'Errors',\n        description: (\n          <UploadDataNotificationContainer>\n            {errorAlerts.map((alertMessage, index) => (\n              <p key={index}>{alertMessage}</p>\n            ))}\n          </UploadDataNotificationContainer>\n        ),\n        duration: 0,\n        onClose: () => setErrorAlerts([]),\n      });\n  }, [errorAlerts]);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    setSelectedIds([]);\n  }, [activeTab, filterData]);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (uploadId) {\n      getUploadStatus(uploadId);\n\n      timer = setInterval(() => {\n        getUploadStatus(uploadId);\n      }, 1000 * 5);\n    } else {\n      if (timer) clearInterval(timer as unknown as number);\n    }\n\n    return () => {\n      if (timer && !uploadId) clearInterval(timer as unknown as number);\n    };\n  }, [uploadId, getUploadStatus]);\n\n  const items = useMemo(() => {\n    const items = [\n      {\n        key: 'pending_upload',\n        label: (\n          <TabBadge\n            tabTitle='Pending for upload'\n            tabBadge={viewType !== 'invoice' ? 0 : tabCount || 0}\n          />\n        ),\n        children: activeTab === 'pending_upload' && (\n          <PendingUpload\n            form={form}\n            isGstr1A={isGstr1A}\n            selectedIds={selectedIds}\n            setSelectedIds={setSelectedIds}\n            setTabsCount={setTabsCount}\n            viewType={viewType}\n            isButtonDisabled={isButtonDisabled || false}\n            setViewType={setViewType}\n            reloadData={reloadPendingUpload}\n            setInvoiceType={setInvoiceType}\n            setExportFilter={setFilterData}\n            setUploadId={setUploadId}\n            invoiceType={invoiceType!}\n            uploadId={uploadId}\n          />\n        ),\n      },\n    ];\n    if (isPermissionAllowed(APPModules.GSTR1, GSTR1Access.UploadHistoryView))\n      items.push({\n        key: 'history',\n        label: <TabBadge tabTitle='Upload History' />,\n        children: activeTab === 'history' && (\n          <UploadHistory\n            isGstr1A={isGstr1A}\n            uploadId={uploadId!}\n            isButtonDisabled={isButtonDisabled}\n            setReloadPendingUpload={setReloadPendingUpload}\n          />\n        ),\n      });\n    isPermissionAllowed(APPModules.GSTR1, GSTR1Access.CompareDataView);\n    items.push({\n      key: 'compare',\n      label: <TabBadge tabTitle='Compare Data' />,\n      children: activeTab === 'compare' && (\n        <CompareData isGstr1A={isGstr1A} isButtonDisabled={isButtonDisabled} />\n      ),\n    });\n    return items;\n  }, [\n    activeTab,\n    isGstr1A,\n    reloadPendingUpload,\n    selectedIds,\n    tabCount,\n    viewType,\n    uploadId,\n  ]);\n\n  return (\n    <UploadDataContainer>\n      {!!uploadId && (\n        <Beforeunload onBeforeunload={() => 'You’ll lose your data!'} />\n      )}\n      <AppTabs\n        type='card'\n        activeKey={activeTab}\n        onTabClick={setActiveTab}\n        items={items}\n      />\n      {contextHolder}\n    </UploadDataContainer>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default UploadGSTR1Data;\n",
        "libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Gstr6/UploadData/index.tsx": "import React, { useCallback, useEffect, useMemo, useState } from 'react';\nimport { UploadDataContainer, UploadDataNotificationContainer } from './index.styled';\n\nimport AppTabs from '@mi/components/AppTabs';\nimport { APPModules } from '@mi/constants/AppEnums';\nimport { GSTR6Access } from '@mi/constants/permissions/app/returns/GSTR6';\nimport { useInfoViewActionsContext } from '@mi/context/AppInfoViewContextProvider';\nimport { getDataApi } from '@mi/hooks/APIHooks';\nimport useManagePermission from '@mi/hooks/useManagePermission';\nimport { UploadStatusProps } from '@mi/models/GstReturns/Gstr1/Prepare';\nimport { notification } from 'antd';\nimport { Beforeunload } from 'react-beforeunload';\nimport TabBadge from '../../components/TabBadge';\nimport PendingUpload from './PendingUpload';\nimport UploadHistory from './UploadHistory';\n\nexport type Gstr6UploadFilterProps = {\n  search: string;\n  invoice_type: string | null;\n};\n\nlet timer: NodeJS.Timer;\nexport const UploadGSTR6Data = () => {\n  const infoViewContext = useInfoViewActionsContext();\n\n  const [activeTab, setActiveTab] = useState('pending_upload');\n  const [tabCount, setTabsCount] = useState<number | null>(null);\n  const [uploadId, setUploadId] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  const [reloadPendingUpload, setReloadPendingUpload] = useState(false);\n  const [successAlerts, setSuccessAlerts] = useState<string[]>([]);\n  const [errorAlerts, setErrorAlerts] = useState<string[]>([]);\n  const { isPermissionAllowed } = useManagePermission();\n  const [api, contextHolder] = notification.useNotification();\n  const hasUploadPermission = isPermissionAllowed(\n    APPModules.GSTR6,\n    GSTR6Access.UploadHistory,\n  );\n  const getUploadStatus = useCallback((id: string) => {\n    getDataApi<UploadStatusProps>(\n      'gst-returns/gstr6/upload/status/',\n      infoViewContext,\n      { id },\n      true,\n    )\n      .then((response) => {\n        if (response.data.status === 'done') {\n          setUploadId(null);\n          setReloadPendingUpload(true);\n          sessionStorage.removeItem('upload_id');\n          const success: string[] = [];\n          const errors: string[] = [];\n\n          response.data?.alerts?.forEach((alert) => {\n            if (alert?.status) {\n              success.push(\n                `${alert?.invoice_type?.toUpperCase()}: ${alert?.message}`,\n              );\n            } else {\n              errors.push(\n                `${alert?.invoice_type?.toUpperCase()}: ${alert?.message}`,\n              );\n            }\n          });\n\n          setSuccessAlerts(success);\n          setErrorAlerts(errors);\n        }\n      })\n      .catch((error) => {\n        infoViewContext.fetchError(error.message);\n        setUploadId(null);\n        setReloadPendingUpload(true);\n        sessionStorage.removeItem('upload_id');\n      });\n  }, []);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const upload_id = sessionStorage.getItem('upload_id');\n    if (upload_id) setUploadId(upload_id);\n  }, []);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (reloadPendingUpload) {\n      setTimeout(() => {\n        setReloadPendingUpload(false);\n      }, 1000);\n    }\n  }, [reloadPendingUpload]);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (successAlerts.length > 0)\n      api.success({\n        message: 'Success',\n        description: (\n          <UploadDataNotificationContainer>\n            {successAlerts.map((alertMessage, index) => (\n              <p key={index}>{alertMessage}</p>\n            ))}\n          </UploadDataNotificationContainer>\n        ),\n        duration: 0,\n        onClose: () => setSuccessAlerts([]),\n      });\n  }, [successAlerts]);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (errorAlerts.length > 0)\n      api.error({\n        message: 'Errors',\n        description: (\n          <UploadDataNotificationContainer>\n            {errorAlerts.map((alertMessage, index) => (\n              <p key={index}>{alertMessage}</p>\n            ))}\n          </UploadDataNotificationContainer>\n        ),\n        duration: 0,\n        onClose: () => setErrorAlerts([]),\n      });\n  }, [errorAlerts]);\n\n\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (uploadId) {\n      getUploadStatus(uploadId);\n\n      timer = setInterval(() => {\n        getUploadStatus(uploadId);\n      }, 1000 * 5);\n    } else {\n      if (timer) clearInterval(timer as unknown as number);\n    }\n\n    return () => {\n      if (timer && !uploadId) clearInterval(timer as unknown as number);\n    };\n  }, [uploadId, getUploadStatus]);\n\n  const items = useMemo(\n    () => [\n      {\n        key: 'pending_upload',\n        label: (\n          <TabBadge tabTitle='Pending for upload' tabBadge={tabCount || 0} />\n        ),\n        children: activeTab === 'pending_upload' && (\n          <PendingUpload\n            setTabsCount={setTabsCount}\n            reloadPendingUpload={reloadPendingUpload}\n            uploadId={uploadId}\n            setUploadId={setUploadId}\n            setReloadPendingUpload={setReloadPendingUpload}\n          />\n        ),\n      },\n      {\n        key: 'history',\n        label: <TabBadge tabTitle='Upload History' />,\n        children: activeTab === 'history' && (\n          <UploadHistory uploadId={uploadId!} />\n        ),\n      },\n    ],\n    [\n      reloadPendingUpload,\n      tabCount,\n      // selectedIds,\n      activeTab,\n      // refreshData,\n      uploadId,\n    ],\n  );\n\n  return (\n    <UploadDataContainer>\n      {!!uploadId && (\n        <Beforeunload onBeforeunload={() => 'You’ll lose your data!'} />\n      )}\n      <AppTabs\n        type='card'\n        activeKey={activeTab}\n        onTabClick={setActiveTab}\n        // tabBarExtraContent={getTabHeader()}\n        items={items}\n      />\n      {contextHolder}\n    </UploadDataContainer>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default React.memo(UploadGSTR6Data);\n",
        "libs/smb/src/lib/gst/Gstr7/UploadData/index.tsx": "import { useInfoViewActionsContext } from '@mi/context/AppInfoViewContextProvider';\nimport { notification } from 'antd';\nimport { useCallback, useEffect, useMemo, useState } from 'react';\nimport { Beforeunload } from 'react-beforeunload';\nimport PendingUpload from './PendingUpload';\n\nimport AppTabs from '@mi/components/AppTabs';\nimport { APPModules } from '@mi/constants/AppEnums';\nimport { getDataApi } from '@mi/hooks/APIHooks';\nimport useManagePermission from '@mi/hooks/useManagePermission';\nimport { UploadStatusProps } from '@mi/models/GstReturns/Gstr1/Prepare';\nimport { GSTR1Access } from '@mi/permissions/returns/GSTR1';\nimport { UploadDataContainer, UploadDataNotificationContainer } from '../../Gstr1/UploadData/index.styled';\nimport UploadHistory from '../ViewData/UploadHistory';\n\nlet timer: NodeJS.Timer;\n\nexport type FilterProps = {\n  search: string;\n  invoice_type: string | null;\n};\n\ntype Props = {\n  isGstr1A?: boolean;\n  isButtonDisabled?: boolean;\n};\nexport const UploadGSTR7Data = ({ isButtonDisabled }: Props) => {\n  const infoViewContext = useInfoViewActionsContext();\n  const [activeTab, setActiveTab] = useState('pending_upload');\n  const [viewType, setViewType] = useState('detail');\n  const [uploadId, setUploadId] = useState<string | null>(null);\n  const [successAlerts, setSuccessAlerts] = useState<string[]>([]);\n  const [errorAlerts, setErrorAlerts] = useState<string[]>([]);\n  const { isPermissionAllowed } = useManagePermission();\n  const [api, contextHolder] = notification.useNotification();\n  const getUploadStatus = useCallback((id: string) => {\n    getDataApi<UploadStatusProps>(\n      'gst-returns/gstr7/upload/status/',\n      infoViewContext,\n      { id },\n      true,\n    )\n      .then((response) => {\n        if (response.data.status === 'done') {\n          setUploadId(null);\n          sessionStorage.removeItem('upload_id');\n          const success: string[] = [];\n          const errors: string[] = [];\n\n          response.data?.alerts?.forEach((alert) => {\n            if (alert?.status) {\n              success.push(\n                `${alert?.invoice_type?.toUpperCase()}: ${alert?.message}`,\n              );\n            } else {\n              errors.push(\n                `${alert?.invoice_type?.toUpperCase()}: ${alert?.message}`,\n              );\n            }\n          });\n\n          setSuccessAlerts(success);\n          setErrorAlerts(errors);\n        }\n      })\n      .catch((error) => {\n        infoViewContext.fetchError(error.message);\n        setUploadId(null);\n        sessionStorage.removeItem('upload_id');\n      });\n  }, []);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const upload_id = sessionStorage.getItem('upload_id');\n    if (upload_id) setUploadId(upload_id);\n  }, []);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (successAlerts.length > 0)\n      api.success({\n        message: 'Success',\n        description: (\n          <UploadDataNotificationContainer>\n            {successAlerts.map((alertMessage, index) => (\n              <p key={index}>{alertMessage}</p>\n            ))}\n          </UploadDataNotificationContainer>\n        ),\n        duration: 0,\n        onClose: () => setSuccessAlerts([]),\n      });\n  }, [successAlerts]);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (errorAlerts.length > 0)\n      api.error({\n        message: 'Errors',\n        description: (\n          <UploadDataNotificationContainer>\n            {errorAlerts.map((alertMessage, index) => (\n              <p key={index}>{alertMessage}</p>\n            ))}\n          </UploadDataNotificationContainer>\n        ),\n        duration: 0,\n        onClose: () => setErrorAlerts([]),\n      });\n  }, [errorAlerts]);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (uploadId) {\n      getUploadStatus(uploadId);\n\n      timer = setInterval(() => {\n        getUploadStatus(uploadId);\n      }, 1000 * 5);\n    } else {\n      if (timer) clearInterval(timer as unknown as number);\n    }\n\n    return () => {\n      if (timer && !uploadId) clearInterval(timer as unknown as number);\n    };\n  }, [uploadId, getUploadStatus]);\n\n  const items = useMemo(() => {\n    const items = [\n      {\n        key: 'pending_upload',\n        label: 'Pending for upload',\n        children: activeTab === 'pending_upload' && (\n          <PendingUpload\n            viewType={viewType}\n            isButtonDisabled={isButtonDisabled || false}\n            setViewType={setViewType}\n            setUploadId={setUploadId}\n            uploadId={uploadId}\n          />\n        ),\n      },\n    ];\n    if (isPermissionAllowed(APPModules.GSTR1, GSTR1Access.UploadHistoryView))\n      items.push({\n        key: 'history',\n        label: 'Upload History',\n        children: activeTab === 'history' && (\n          <UploadHistory uploadId={uploadId!} />\n        ),\n      });\n    return items;\n  }, [\n    activeTab,\n    viewType,\n    uploadId,\n  ]);\n\n  return (\n    <UploadDataContainer>\n      {!!uploadId && (\n        <Beforeunload onBeforeunload={() => 'You’ll lose your data!'} />\n      )}\n      <AppTabs\n        type='card'\n        activeKey={activeTab}\n        onTabClick={setActiveTab}\n        items={items}\n      />\n      {contextHolder}\n    </UploadDataContainer>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default UploadGSTR7Data;\n",
        "package.json": "{\n  \"name\": \"mi\",\n  \"version\": \"0.0.0\",\n  \"license\": \"MIT\",\n  \"scripts\": {},\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@nx/eslint-plugin\": \"22.0.4\",\n    \"@nx/jest\": \"^21.2.4\",\n    \"@nx/js\": \"22.0.4\",\n    \"@nx/react\": \"22.0.4\",\n    \"@nx/vite\": \"22.0.4\",\n    \"@nx/workspace\": \"22.0.4\",\n    \"@testing-library/react\": \"16.3.0\",\n    \"@types/jest\": \"30.0.0\",\n    \"@types/lodash\": \"4.17.20\",\n    \"@types/node\": \"24.10.1\",\n    \"@types/react\": \"^19.2.6\",\n    \"@types/react-dom\": \"^19.2.3\",\n    \"@types/react-highlight-words\": \"0.20.0\",\n    \"@types/react-is\": \"19.2.0\",\n    \"@types/turndown\": \"^5.0.6\",\n    \"@types/validator\": \"^13.15.10\",\n    \"@typescript-eslint/eslint-plugin\": \"8.47.0\",\n    \"@typescript-eslint/parser\": \"8.47.0\",\n    \"@vitejs/plugin-react\": \"^5.1.1\",\n    \"@vitest/ui\": \"^4.0.10\",\n    \"eslint\": \"9.39.1\",\n    \"eslint-plugin-import\": \"2.32.0\",\n    \"eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y\": \"6.10.2\",\n    \"eslint-plugin-react\": \"7.37.5\",\n    \"eslint-plugin-react-hooks\": \"7.0.1\",\n    \"jest\": \"^29.7.0\",\n    \"jsdom\": \"^27.2.0\",\n    \"nx\": \"22.0.4\",\n    \"nx-cloud\": \"19.1.0\",\n    \"prettier\": \"3.6.2\",\n    \"react-refresh\": \"0.18.0\",\n    \"ts-jest\": \"29.4.5\",\n    \"typescript\": \"5.9.3\",\n    \"url-loader\": \"4.1.1\",\n    \"vite\": \"^7.2.2\",\n    \"vite-plugin-dts\": \"4.5.4\",\n    \"vite-plugin-mkcert\": \"^1.17.9\",\n    \"vite-plugin-svgr\": \"^4.5.0\",\n    \"vitest\": \"^4.0.10\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@ant-design/icons\": \"6.1.0\",\n    \"@ant-design/pro-components\": \"3.1.3-1\",\n    \"@azure/msal-browser\": \"^4.26.1\",\n    \"@azure/msal-react\": \"^3.0.21\",\n    \"@builder.io/partytown\": \"0.10.3\",\n    \"@dnd-kit/core\": \"^6.3.1\",\n    \"@dnd-kit/modifiers\": \"^9.0.0\",\n    \"@dnd-kit/sortable\": \"^10.0.0\",\n    \"@faker-js/faker\": \"^10.1.0\",\